# Arcades Profile — Cursor Rules

## Tech stack
- Next.js 16 (App Router), React 19, TypeScript (strict)
- Repository-owned Markdown content — no database, no CMS
- Tailwind CSS + SASS
- Vercel deployment

## Package manager
Always use **npm**. Never suggest `yarn`, `pnpm`, or `bun`.

## Code style
- TypeScript strict mode — no `any` unless absolutely necessary
- Prefer functional components and React hooks
- Co-locate types with the files that use them
- Use Tailwind utility classes; avoid inline styles

## Project conventions
- App Router pages live under `app/(frontend)/`
- Public essays are `content/posts/<group>/<slug>.md`, one `_group.json` manifest per group
- Private drafts live in `content/drafts`
- Frontmatter is strict and validated by `lib/markdown-posts.ts`; `publishDate` is the only visibility control
- Shared utilities belong in `lib/`
- All new API routes go under `app/(frontend)/api/`

## Commands
- `npm run dev` — start dev server (port 3000)
- `npm run lint` — ESLint
- `npm test` — run tests with tsx
- `npm run build` — production build

## Environment
- Required vars are in `.env.example` — never commit real secrets
